00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:09.200
Appeal Scoring Sheet

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.580
Oh, I see.

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:09.330
Each photo is scored on a 
fifteen step scale, right?

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:13.100
Please, feel free to score my 
magnificent appearance highly.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:17.580
Oh! And you have a ranking of the 
current attractiveness scores!

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:21.090
<b>2nd</b>

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:19.710
Himuro-san?

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:21.100
She's adorable!

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:24.340
<b>Score</b>

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:24.340
<b>1st</b>

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:23.100
And first is...

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.340
Who is that?

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:27.330
The person is very beautiful, but...

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:32.110
Oh, miss! What do you think 
of that cosplay over there?

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.600
Wow!

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:38.090
Ena, you're beautiful!

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:41.330
May I take a picture? I can, can't I?

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:45.120
I just knew it, Ena-senpai! 
You're super-lovely!

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:48.610
Ugh. Why are you here, manga artist?

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:51.170
What is it?

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:55.360
These guys forced me to wear this.

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:57.960
Could it be you find me captivating?

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.040
Wha?!

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:00.890
Of course not, you moron!

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:03.370
<i>Hey, hang on.</i>

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:05.540
<i>Doesn't this make it...</i>

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:08.380
<i>seem like the two of us are getting married?!</i>

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:11.280
It's so wonderful. A wedding dress.

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.570
Miss, would you like to try it, too?

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:16.130
There aren't many chances to 
wear these sorts of things!

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:18.280
M-M-Me?

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:20.450
N-N-No, I'm fine!

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:24.280
I mean, it wouldn't suit 
someone like me in the least!

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:26.660
Oh, honestly! Not at all!

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:33.650
It looks lovely, miss!

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:37.320
Father, Mother... right now, Arika is

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:39.750
shining the brightest she has in her life!

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:43.670
Now, Kosuke-san, shall we 
go to the ceremony hall?

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:46.000
Won't you please make me happy?

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:48.500
Huh? No, um...

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:51.420
Why are you casually trying to get married?

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:54.860
What is it, Ena? Might you be jealous?

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:56.700
Of course not.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:59.160
<i>Is this situation for real?</i>

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:00.700
<i>Setting aside who they are inside...</i>

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:03.760
<i>two lovely brides are fighting over me?</i>

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:05.980
<i>It's like a real life erotic video game!</i>

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:07.820
<i>...setting aside who they are inside.</i>

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:10.140
Oh, I'm so glad you did it!

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:15.070
Not many people are wearing the wedding 
dresses, so we were in a bit of a bind!

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:16.230
What?

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:20.680
"If you wear a wedding dress, the time 
for your own wedding will be delayed."

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:23.580
...or something like that. 
A lot of people were worried about it.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:26.120
But that would never happen, right?

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:28.350
It's just a superstition!

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:29.830
Right?

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:32.340
The Relationship Between
Wedding Dresses and
the Age One Marries

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:36.420
How is it going?

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:39.300
Have you found any evidence 
that wearing a wedding dress

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:41.690
increases the age at which 
someone gets married?

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:44.620
I haven't found anything yet.

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:45.830
Basically,

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:49.340
if we had the ages of those who'd worn a 
wedding dress prior to getting married

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:55.630
and ages of those who didn't for a 
statistical data analysis, we could verify it.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:55.620
<b>How old were you when you got married?</b>

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:58.400
But if such precise data existed...

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:00.860
I would cry.

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:03.540
No... Hang on.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:07.930
Even if the average age of marriage 
for those who'd worn a wedding dress

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:14.130
<b>Wore a Wedding Dress</b>

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:14.130
<b>Did Not Wear</b>

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:14.130
<b>Age
of
Marriage</b>

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:12.020
was clearly higher than that of those 
who did not wear a wedding dress...

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:14.120
Suppose we had that data.

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:19.480
That would not mean that wearing the wedding 
dress delayed the timing of their weddings.

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:20.630
That's true!

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:24.160
The causal relationships and 
correlations are mixed together.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:29.880
For example, say there was data that areas 
with more police boxes had more crime.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:33.290
Then, would crime decrease if 
there were fewer police boxes?

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:34.870
No.

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:39.970
Why? Because they built a lot of 
police boxes due to all the crime.

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:41.890
In just the same way...

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:44.420
<b>A lot
of crime</b>

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:44.420
<b>A lot
of police boxes</b>

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:44.420
<b>Married
Late</b>

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:44.420
<b>Wore a
Wedding Dress</b>

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:44.400
in short, in this case...

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:48.480
it could be that it wasn't that they married 
late because they wore a wedding dress...

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:55.930
<b>Chances to Wear a Wedding Dress</b>

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:55.930
<b>People Who
Wore One</b>

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:55.930
<b>People Who
Didn't
Wear One</b>

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:55.930
<b>Wedding</b>

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:55.930
<b>Wedding</b>

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:55.930
<b>Number
of Years</b>

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:55.930
<b>Age
at Marriage</b>

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:55.930
<b>Age
at Marriage</b>

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:55.930
<b>Born</b>

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:51.510
but because they married late,

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:56.010
they had more opportunities 
to wear a wedding dress.

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:59.270
In which case, it means...

00:08:59.270 --> 00:09:01.490
that there can be no definitive 
proof that wearing a wedding dress

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:03.430
delays the date of your wedding.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:05.560
All right! I'm safe!

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:12.190
The Relationship Between
Wedding Dresses and
the Age One Marries

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:08.030
I'm fine even though I wore one! Probably!

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:12.190
Well, it's not like I care 
about getting married anyway.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:15.430
Seriously, though... 
This is who they are inside...

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:18.860
I mean, you really want to 
get married that badly?

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:20.320
Is it because you're around thirty?

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:21.890
Shut up!

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:23.820
You probably wouldn't understand, Ena.

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:27.530
But my thirties are closing in! 
My friends are getting married!

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:30.940
The pressure I feel to get married from 
my parents whenever I visit...

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:32.890
I spend every day locked up 
in my room drawing manga.

00:09:32.890 --> 00:09:34.840
There's no way for me to meet anyone!

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:38.090
When I see myself in the mirror the 
morning after pulling an all-nighter...

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:42.840
I think, "I'm done as a woman," 
and I lament it every day.

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:47.780
Today, I am the most beautiful 
I have ever been in my life!

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:50.370
Someone, it doesn't matter who, 
please marry me!

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:52.040
Okay, Kosuke-san?

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:54.360
Whoa, that's scary! I'm scared!

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:58.260
Someone save me!

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:57.500
Wait, Kosuke-san!

00:09:57.500 --> 00:10:01.470
Hurry up and provide for me, please!

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:04.620
You're not going to stop her, Ena-senpai?

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:07.350
She's going to make Kosuke-san marry her.

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:10.510
Nope. It's not my problem.

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:20.500
Hey, Kosuke! Have you seen Kanade?

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:22.760
This is no time for that!

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:24.550
What is he in such a panic about?

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:27.520
Wedding. Wedding. Wedding. Wedding. Wedding. 
Wedding. Wedding. Wedding. Wedding.

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:27.520
Hey! Manga artist!

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:30.570
Please provide for me!

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:32.810
Wh-What are they doing?

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:35.280
That looks really good on you!

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:42.430
Oh, man. Looks like I managed to lose her.

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:44.920
Being too popular can be such a problem.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:51.150
I stand out surprisingly little, 
even in this outfit.

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:54.260
And there are a lot of people dressed 
weirdly during the festival.

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:56.290
What? It's just you?

00:10:56.620 --> 00:10:58.290
What did you come here for?

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:00.800
Hey, Torasuke...

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:05.690
I've walked too much in these 
wedding shoes. My feet hurt.

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:07.020
I can't move anymore.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:09.570
Seriously! What did you come here for?!

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:11.600
Honestly, you...

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:12.920
Oh!

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:16.820
A bride! There's a bride here!

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:19.060
What a pretty bride.

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:20.940
I-I'm so sorry.

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:23.520
This girl really admires brides.

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:26.830
Miss! Mister! Are you getting married?

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:28.090
Wha?!

00:11:28.090 --> 00:11:29.670
N-No, we're not!

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:31.420
Who'd marry this pipsqueak woman?!

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:34.350
You're not?

00:11:34.350 --> 00:11:37.350
Divorce? Are you divorced?

00:11:37.350 --> 00:11:40.650
What?! No, it's not... Um...

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:44.120
Look at that. Don't crush children's dreams.

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:48.110
We are getting married. Right after this.

00:11:48.110 --> 00:11:49.010
Really?

00:11:49.010 --> 00:11:52.280
Yes. Do you want to get married one day?

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:53.090
Yeah!

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:55.270
Then, look closely.

00:11:55.600 --> 00:12:00.050
Weddings take a lot of money, 
and preparations are a lot of work.

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:03.620
The dress binds you up so tightly 
it'll make you feel like throwing up.

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:08.460
Right now, I'm wearing a tulle-filled 
pannier skirt, so it's not too bad,

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:14.340
but there are stupidly large, one-meter wide, 
six-hoop wire frames for these things.

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:19.140
They're heavy, so you can't really walk, 
you can't sit, you can't even use the toilet.

00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:23.120
You're the one taking the 
lead in crushing her dreams!

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:28.650
In spite of all that, being able to 
be with Kosuke makes me truly happy.

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:35.360
For better or worse, for richer or poorer,

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:36.140
<i>Stop it.</i>

00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:41.590
in sickness and in health, 
to love and to cherish.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:47.950
<b>Saitama University
Wind Ensemble</b>

00:12:47.940 --> 00:12:54.340
and I promise to be faithful 
to you until death do us part.

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:50.510
<i>Stop doing stuff like this.</i>

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:52.150
<i>Seriously.</i>

00:12:54.950 --> 00:12:56.910
<i>This is wrong!</i>

00:12:56.910 --> 00:13:01.000
<i>My dream is to marry Aika.</i>

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:02.460
<i>Absolutely not...</i>

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:04.960
<i>a pipsqueak woman like her!</i>

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:06.250
<i>Someone like...</i>

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:09.260
So, what will you do?

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:12.220
Will you kiss me?

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:15.750
<i>What? You can't be serious! Who'd do—</i>

00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:18.540
Torasuke.

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:20.240
<i>Stop it, you little—!</i>

00:13:20.890 --> 00:13:24.230
I'd never do that, would I? Idiot.

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:41.690
Miss! Mister! Thank you!

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:47.140
Wasn't that wonderful?

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:47.860
Yeah!

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:50.260
Ena! Where are you?

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:53.370
Let's go around the festival together!

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:57.410
I won't pressure Kosuke-san to 
marry me anymore, all right?

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:09.020
My feet hurt. I shouldn't have 
done that ridiculous stuff.

00:14:09.020 --> 00:14:11.530
You planted those seeds 
yourself, didn't you?

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:14.730
Marriage is just something a 
person shouldn't do, right?

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:18.530
I don't think I'll be able 
to walk back to the lab.

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:21.810
<i>This woman is always like this.</i>

00:14:22.140 --> 00:14:26.290
<i>She's always lazing around, 
poking fun at people.</i>

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:30.810
<i>And yet, when no one's looking, she'll push 
herself hard and make little adjustments.</i>

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:34.820
<i>When I'm feeling down, 
she'll go and drag me back up.</i>

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:41.070
Come on, Torasuke. Escort me back properly.

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:43.220
<i>What is she?</i>

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:45.150
<i>I don't know anymore!</i>

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:49.080
<i>What do I think of this woman?</i>

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:06.600
Your face is so red!

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:10.330
You're much too flustered.

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:13.270
Our lips just brushed 
together a little, right?

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:15.770
And it's just me, anyway.

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:18.080
We're not middle schoolers here.

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.860
Sh-Shut up!

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:23.340
You'd do this much with someone 
the same gender, right?

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:24.900
Like Yukimura, for example.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:26.240
No, I wouldn't!

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:29.250
Don't think I'm the same as you 
in your high school years!

00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:31.700
Huh... You're such a child.

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:34.980
If you're behaving like that, 
you won't be able to escort me, will you?

00:15:34.980 --> 00:15:38.000
You! You're walking just fine!

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:41.440
I suppose it can't be helped. 
I'll get back on my own.

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:44.360
Blast it. You've gotta be 
kidding me, you little—!

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:46.970
<i>You might be fine...</i>

00:15:47.540 --> 00:15:49.210
<i>but I'm...</i>

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:51.510
<i>I'm not in that state at all!</i>

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:06.290
<i>Oh, man...</i>

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:11.910
Science Fell in Love,
So I Tried to Prove It [<b>r=1-sinθ</b>]

00:16:14.710 --> 00:16:16.700
Thank you, everyone!

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:22.820
And thank you so much for taking the trouble 
to travel so far to be here today,

00:16:22.820 --> 00:16:25.210
Professor Kanou, Professor Kaku.

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:29.210
No, thank you. 
I've had a very good time.

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:34.820
The universities in China don't have 
festivals like this, so it's new to me.

00:16:34.820 --> 00:16:38.430
The atmosphere on a festival 
night is nice, too.

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:40.460
The ban on alcohol is lifted 
at night, after all.

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:44.340
Lately, the number of school festivals which 
regulate food and drink has increased.

00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:49.330
Soon, the illumination display that the 
Kaihori Lab created is going to start.

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:50.500
Really?

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:54.650
Professor Kaihori does something 
interesting every time, don't you think?

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:55.410
<b>Super-Popular
Takoyaki</b>

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:59.370
<b>Super-Popular
Takoyaki</b>

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:02.370
That's...

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:05.340
<i>Kanade-chan.</i>

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:09.100
<i>I was just thinking that I hadn't seen her. 
She was with Shikijou-kun.</i>

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:12.280
<i>I shouldn't intrude.</i>

00:17:16.340 --> 00:17:19.940
<i>Kanade-chan... I hope everything 
goes well for her.</i>

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:23.680
Man, those kebabs were 
delicious, weren't they?

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:26.410
We have them every year here 
at the Mutsumi Festival.

00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:28.770
Wow. Really?

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:31.230
I hope I can come again next year.

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:33.900
Please do! Come and have fun!

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:37.650
Thank you for showing me around 
to all the different places today.

00:17:37.650 --> 00:17:38.880
Not at all!

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:42.920
I'm glad I got to look around the 
Mutsumi Festival with you, Shikijou-kun.

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:46.140
We'll be having a festival 
at our university, too.

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:47.660
Would you like to come?

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:49.830
Yes, let's go!

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:52.910
It'll be my first time to Touri U.! 
I'm super looking forward to it!

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:54.500
I-I'm glad you said that.

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:58.340
Our university is all guys, 
so it might be a little... you know?

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:00.800
Oh, I'll go buy us something to drink!

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:07.530
Your face says you're tired.

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:11.940
Doesn't living in blind obedience to 
"the mood" leave you in constant anxiety?

00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:17.220
And who do you think you are?

00:18:17.220 --> 00:18:21.200
You're always looking down on people, 
thrusting logical arguments at people.

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:24.180
You don't understand people's feelings,

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:26.720
and you are unrelenting in your rationalism.

00:18:26.950 --> 00:18:30.410
I can't live like you, Yukimura-senpai.

00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:33.600
If my alternative is to become 
a science-type like you,

00:18:33.600 --> 00:18:36.210
then being a normal slave is enough for me!

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:40.680
Kanade, there's something 
I want to say to you.

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:41.610
Hey!

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:46.220
She is very important to me.

00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:48.460
Do you have some business with her?

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:51.470
Let's go, Kanade-san.

00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:53.990
Do you know him?

00:18:54.890 --> 00:18:56.480
No, I don't.

00:18:58.490 --> 00:18:59.480
Hey! Wait!

00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:05.860
What was that? 
Did he fail at hitting on her?

00:19:07.220 --> 00:19:08.290
Tch.

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:10.830
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:12.670
<i>I'm sorry!</i>

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:17.330
<i>Why do I end up saying things 
like that to that person?</i>

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:20.210
<i>The truth is, I know.</i>

00:19:20.990 --> 00:19:24.560
<i>He always butts heads with 
me with everything he's got.</i>

00:19:25.170 --> 00:19:28.030
<i>He's saying all of that 
for my sake, that's all.</i>

00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:32.300
<i>I've learned so much from him.</i>

00:19:33.140 --> 00:19:34.600
<i>And now...</i>

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:36.630
<i>I'm sure he's abandoned me, but...</i>

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:38.910
<i>But this was for the best.</i>

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:44.690
What are you doing, Yukimura-kun?

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:46.250
You were watching, Himuro?

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:49.790
It looked like a boyfriend chasing off 
a guy trying to hit on his girlfriend.

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:54.980
You said something that rubbed Kanade-chan 
the wrong way again, didn't you?

00:19:56.660 --> 00:19:59.680
By the way, did you finish getting 
those documents together?

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:00.820
Yes.

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:02.370
I see.

00:20:02.370 --> 00:20:07.180
But I think it might be best 
to just let her be for today.

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:11.180
So, come, Yukimura-kun.

00:20:11.450 --> 00:20:14.430
Let's go see the illumination display.

00:20:14.730 --> 00:20:17.930
Y-Yes. You're right.

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:20.580
They say that the Kaihori Lab built it.

00:20:21.140 --> 00:20:23.760
It reacts to the movements of the 
people watching, and to sounds.

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:25.270
It's interactive.

00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:28.890
It's just like that lab to 
come up with that idea.

00:20:32.970 --> 00:20:35.760
<i>I can't live like that person...</i>

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:40.960
<i>because there's someone who 
wants the "normal" me.</i>

00:20:41.930 --> 00:20:43.040
Kanade-san.

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:45.840
I'd like you to allow me to ask you again...

00:20:46.110 --> 00:20:49.110
Would you... go out with me?

00:20:52.070 --> 00:20:54.870
<i>He's nice enough to fall in 
love with someone like me.</i>

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:57.120
<i>I have to respond to him.</i>

00:20:57.450 --> 00:21:00.630
<i>Yukimura-senpai has Himuro-senpai.</i>

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:04.110
<i>And I'm sure that they'll continue, 
strong, unwavering,</i>

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:07.480
<i>doing their ridiculous research like always.</i>

00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:11.120
<i>There's no need for them 
to look after me anymore.</i>

00:21:11.530 --> 00:21:15.910
<i>Shikijou-san will be happy,
and so will my mom and dad! I just know it!</i>

00:21:15.910 --> 00:21:17.770
<i>That's the best thing to have happen!</i>

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:20.330
<i>If everyone is happy...</i>

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:21.960
<i>then I...</i>

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:26.890
I'm sorry.

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:27.830
What?

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:29.550
<i>Huh?</i>

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:34.920
Oh. I see.

00:21:34.920 --> 00:21:37.920
I thought that with the way things 
were going, you'd say okay.

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:43.840
<i>Why did I do that?</i>

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:46.600
Huh? Why, Kanade-san?

00:21:47.770 --> 00:21:50.500
No, you're lying, right?

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:52.760
It's not normal, not after coming this far.

00:21:52.760 --> 00:21:55.860
Huh? Did I do something wrong?

00:21:55.860 --> 00:21:58.760
If there's something you 
don't like, then tell me.

00:21:58.760 --> 00:21:59.880
Kanade-san.

00:22:00.300 --> 00:22:02.780
Come on, Kanade-san.

00:22:02.780 --> 00:22:04.150
Kanade-san!

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.930
Next Time

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.930
Proof 12
I Tried to Prove that You
Are Fine Just as You Are.

00:23:35.320 --> 00:23:37.040
Next time, Proof 12.

00:23:37.040 --> 00:23:40.030
"I Tried to Prove that You 
Are Fine Just as You Are."
